  "rawText": "LLLP\n@ @ cous ciauve Francis @ @\n\nD.O.B.-: December Sh 1925\nPEACE: Halifax County, North Carolina\n\nMOTHER: Pearl C. Francis\n\nFATHER: James H. Francis\nBIRTH ORDER: Thixteenth child\n\nOCCUPATION: Retired Farmer\n\nHOBBIES OR INTERESTS: hunting, fishing, reading and\nwatching sports on TV. He was always eager to\ntry out new and s4nnovative ideas in Agriculture\n\nFAVORITE SAYING OR MOTTO: ver St Earst you don't succeed,\n\ntry: and Cry again.\"\nMILITARY SERVICE: Claude completed his high school eduaction\n\nat Bastman High School and entered into the U.S.\n\nArmy on february 2, 1945, where he served three\n\nyears as a Clerk Typist. He was honorably discharged\n\non November 4, 1948. During his tour of duty, he\n\nreceived several decorations and citations.\n\nPHILOSOPHY OF LIFE: Claude firmly believed that taking\n\ncontrol of one's life meant learning to make good\n\nchoices and being resourceful. He also believed that\n\nmastering any task requires trial and error, but, the\n\nkey to successful Living involves perserverence,\nuntil you succeed.\n\nthe ability to try and try again\n\nThis legacy he leaves to his son, Tony and other\n\nyounger members of his family.\nMARITAL STATUS: Married Velma Adams on March 20, £9:53'.\n\nSAAR AAA\n\nMW:\n\na.\nz a :\n- . \"~ -\n\nr’y > ye. - ‘ ‘ \\ i.\n\na\n\n‘\nile | | =\n\n.*» Fat a “. \"—\n\n* 4 . > ~~ 7 .\n1 ae bh. | ae > “aw p<, ie Saline\n\nA ‘ss -\n\n\"7",
  "cleanedText": "LLLP\n@ @ cous ciauve Francis @ @\n\nD.O.B.-: December Sh 1925\nPEACE: Halifax County, North Carolina\n\nMOTHER: Pearl C. Francis\n\nFATHER: James H. Francis\nBIRTH ORDER: Thixteenth child\n\nOCCUPATION: Retired Farmer\n\nHOBBIES OR INTERESTS: hunting, fishing, reading and\nwatching sports on TV. He was always eager to\ntry out new and s4nnovative ideas in Agriculture\n\nFAVORITE SAYING OR MOTTO: ver St Earst you don't succeed,\n\ntry: and Cry again.\"\nMILITARY SERVICE: Claude completed his high school eduaction\n\nat Bastman High School and entered into the U.S.\n\nArmy on february 2, 1945, where he served three\n\nyears as a Clerk Typist. He was honorably discharged\n\non November 4, 1948. During his tour of duty, he\n\nreceived several decorations and citations.\n\nPHILOSOPHY OF LIFE: Claude firmly believed that taking\n\ncontrol of one's life meant learning to make good\n\nchoices and being resourceful. He also believed that\n\nmastering any task requires trial and error, but, the\n\nkey to successful Living involves perserverence,\nuntil you succeed.\n\nthe ability to try and try again\n\nThis legacy he leaves to his son, Tony and other\n\nyounger members of his family.\nMARITAL STATUS: Married Velma Adams on March 20, £9:53'.\n\nSAAR AAA\n\nMW:\n\na.\nz a :\n- . \"~ -\n\nr’y > ye. - ‘ ‘ \\ i.\n\na\n\n‘\nile I I =\n\n.*» Fat a “. \"—\n\n* 4 . > ~~ 7 .\n1 ae bh. I ae > “aw p<, ie Saline\n\nA ‘ss -\n\n\"7",
